      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'You did it! Here''s your information: Uranus is the seventh planet from
    the Sun and is often called an "ice giant" due to its cold temperatures and icy
    composition. It''s unique for rotating on its side, with an axial tilt of about
    98 degrees, which gives it extreme seasons. Uranus has a pale blue-green color
    caused by methane in its atmosphere and features 13 known rings and 27 moons.
    It takes about 84 Earth years to orbit the Sun. Despite being less visually dramatic
    than Neptune, Uranus is equally fascinating due to its odd tilt and subtle features.


'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
