  m_text: "You did it! Here's your information: Neptune is the eighth and farthest
    planet from the Sun in our solar system. It's a deep blue gas giant known for
    its strong winds\u2014the fastest recorded in the solar system. Neptune has a
    thick atmosphere made mostly of hydrogen, helium, and methane, which gives it
    its vivid blue color. It has 14 known moons, with Triton being the largest and
    geologically active. Despite being so far away, Neptune has faint rings and takes
    about 165 Earth years to complete one orbit around the Sun."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
